Vercel Web Analytics Installation and Configuration
====================================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json

### 2. Framework-Specific Configuration
Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Added Analytics import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout (app/layout.tsx)
- Component placed at the end of the `<body>` tag, following best practices

## Files Modified

### Created:
None - only modified existing files

### Modified:
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
  - Import statement added at top of file
  - Analytics component added before closing body tag
  
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
  - Version: ^2.0.1
  
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
  - Added 439 new packages for @vercel/analytics

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was integrated following the official Vercel documentation:
1. Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. Identified this as a Next.js App Router project
3. Used the Next.js-specific import path: `@vercel/analytics/next`
4. Placed the component at the end of the body to ensure proper page tracking
5. Preserved all existing code structure and components

The Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views
- Send data to `/_vercel/insights/*` routes after deployment
- Work in both development and production modes

## Verification Performed

✓ ESLint passed with no errors on the modified layout.tsx file
✓ Package successfully installed via npm
✓ Lock file (package-lock.json) properly updated
✓ Code structure and imports preserved
✓ No TypeScript errors introduced

Note: Build test encountered a pre-existing error related to Supabase URL configuration, 
which is unrelated to the Analytics installation. The Analytics implementation itself is 
correct and follows official documentation.

## Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
   - Navigate to your project in the Vercel dashboard
   - Select "Analytics" in the sidebar
   - Click the "Enable" button
3. After deployment, verify tracking by checking the Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`
4. View analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after gathering visitor traffic
